        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.028,
            0.293,
            0.042,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "A\nB\nC\nD"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.051,
            0.298,
            0.28,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.047,
                0.263,
                0.117,
                0.283
              ],
              "content": "can and could"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.49,
            0.261,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "| I/we/you/they he/she/it | can can't (cannot) | do play see come etc. | can | I/we/you/they he/she/it | do? play? see? come? etc. |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.047,
                0.474,
                0.17,
                0.488
              ],
              "content": "can + infinitive (can do / can play / can come etc.)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_table_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.562,
            0.218,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "I can do something = I know how to do it, or it is possible for me to do it."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.577,
            0.214,
            0.669
          ],
          "sub_type": "text",
          "content": "I can play the piano. My brother can play the piano too.\nSarah can speak Italian, but she can't speak Spanish.\nA: Can you swim?\na: Yes, but I'm not a very good swimmer.\n☐ A: Can you change twenty pounds?\nB: I'm sorry, I can't.\nI'm having a party next week, but Paul and Rachel can't come."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.68,
            0.196,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "For the past (yesterday / last week etc.), we use could couldn't:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.693,
            0.164,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "When I was young, I could run very fast."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.706,
            0.266,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "Before Maria came to Britain, she couldn't understand much English. Now she can understand everything."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.733,
            0.165,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "I was tired last night, but I couldn't sleep."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.746,
            0.208,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "I had a party last week, but Paul and Rachel couldn't come."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.77,
            0.17,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "Can you ... ? Could you ... ? Can I ... ? Could I ... ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.789,
            0.22,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "We use Can you ... ? or Could you ... ? when we ask people to do things."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.803,
            0.235,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": "Can you open the door, please? or Could you open the door, please?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.816,
            0.204,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "Can you wait a moment, please? or Could you wait ... ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.835,
            0.192,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "We use Can I have ... ? or Can I get ... ? to ask for something;"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.849,
            0.194,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Can I have a glass of water, please? or Can I get ...?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.867,
            0.173,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": "Can I ... ? or Could I ... ? = is it OK to do something?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.881,
            0.102,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "Can I sit here?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.893,
            0.154,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": "☐ Tom, could I borrow your umbrella?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.245,
            0.354,
            0.265
          ],
          "level": 2,
